  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 218 AM EST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nBy Sunday afternoon and evening the low pressure system will have \npushed into the northeast with our area under a more zonal flow with \nan area of low pressure over Mexico into the SW and Texas. This \npattern will generally be what we are under through Monday. \nBeginning on Monday the low pressure system begins to track east \ninto the Arklatex but at this time moisture looks on track to stay\nsouth of the area and stick to the Gulf. This will result in rain\nchances less than 10% through mid next week. Temperatures will \ndecrease into the 30s overnight beginning as early as Saturday \nmorning and lasting through at least Tuesday morning. High temps \nwill also lower into the mid to upper 60s this weekend. Rain \nchances may return late next week into next weekend with broad \ntroughing over much of the eastern CONUS potentially bringing in \nmoisture from the west as an area of low pressure pushes into the \ngulf.",
